From: Angelpro09xd <167892325+Angelpro09xd@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sapphire-0299: the boot screen, painted by xnu while it boots (boot-arg sweet_splash)

The shim puts its boot screen's picture on the panel and starts xnu straight away with
sweet_splash=<physical address of the picture>. xnu then:
- draws no log: the early console (sweet_early.c) reads the boot-args itself first thing in arm_init
  and draws only panics, the text console is muted from the first line (the log still goes to the
  persistent ring);
- paints the boot screen itself: the picture as soon as the console exists (by then the panel
  memory is found black), then a thread types the lines out and keeps the frame on the panel (boot
  framebuffer, then AppleCLCD's console frame) until iOS's first frame;
- restarts into recovery when Volume up is held while the boot screen is up (sweet_keys.c), through
  reboot_kernel with the restart mode set to recovery.
Without the boot-arg nothing changes.
